  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "P.Thirumoorthy vs The Food Safety Officer on 20 March, 2024 Author: T.V.Thamilselvi Bench: T.V.Thamilselvi 1 In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated: 20.03.2024 Coram: The Hon'Ble Mrs.Justice T.V.Thamilselvi Crl.Op No. 5965 of 2022 & Crl.MP.Nos. 3314 & 3315 of 2022 1.P.Thirumoorthy ...p 2.M/s. Sakthi Fruit Products, Represented by its authorised person P.Thirumoorthy, son of Palaniswamy Gounder, No.3a, Vettuvapalayam Main Street, Nasiyanur, Erode - 638 107. Vs. The Food Safety Officer, Coimbatore Corporation Section, Code No. 555. 219, Race Course Road, Coimbatore - 641 018. ... Res Prayer : This petition has been filed under Section 482 of Cr.P.C , call for records in S.T.C.No.373 of 2020 on the file of the Honble Magistrate Court No.1 Coimbatore and quash the complaint in Stc No. of 2020. For Petitioner : Mr.M.Rajaraman https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 2 P.Thirumoorthy vs The Food Safety Officer on 20 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/190279574/ 1",
    "facts": "The petitioner herein filed this petition to call for records in S.T.C.No.373 of 2020 on the file of the Honble Judicial Magistrate Court No.1 Coimbatore and quash the complaint in STC No. 373 of 2020. The complainant enquired about Processed Papaya Soaked in Sugar Syrup to the first accused and had taken samples of the said produce and sent the same to the food analyst on 21.12.2018 and the Analyst tested the product from 24.12.2018 ot 16.08.2019 and sent a report on 21.08.2019 stating that sample had added color exceed the defined limit is unsafe. When the report had sent this accused and the second accused had sent a letter that the product had already lost its expiry. The complainant had sought for permission to file case against the accused to the designated officer and the same was granted https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis by the commissioner of Food Safety and hence he filed the above complaint before the Judicial Magistrate No. 1, Coimbatore under the Section 59(i) of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and 190(1)(A) and 200 CPC. Hence, the petitioner filed this petition to quash the said complaint.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
